1
00:00:01,640 --> 00:00:03,600
Please insert coins.

2
00:00:07,920 --> 00:00:11,400
Well, time to slowly get
crushed into oblivion.

3
00:00:16,940 --> 00:00:17,820
Hold up!

4
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:22,648
It seems the nefarious Netherlord can't
see me, which only changes everything.

5
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:25,157
There we go.

6
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:28,300
Next up, I'll cleverly spend
the points I have left.

7
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:31,620
Guess who's good as new?

8
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:42,580
Small call.

9
00:00:43,080 --> 00:00:45,057
These babies are used in dioramas,

10
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:49,140
and according to my research, they're
the smallest vending machines.

11
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:00,720
Boxxo is back!

12
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:03,257
Hopefully the nether dork
thinks I kicked the bucket,

13
00:01:03,340 --> 00:01:06,222
but I'd better camouflage
myself just to be safe.

14
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:14,680
What in the heck?

15
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:17,428
Why'd he make a supersized
summoning circle?

16
00:01:22,020 --> 00:01:23,040
Red alert!

17
00:01:23,320 --> 00:01:25,849
That freak combined
all the Stratum bosses!

18
00:01:26,180 --> 00:01:29,592
Ruh-roh, that means this mad
monster's packing peak power!

19
00:01:34,980 --> 00:01:38,509
It's only a matter of time until
this whole place collapses!

20
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:46,780
Behold, as I entomb that foolish demon
lord and assert control over my own domain!

21
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:52,464
And that's how I wound up living
underground for four whole days.

22
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:55,757
I bunkered up with telekinesis
and concrete blocks,

23
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:57,899
plus flowers for a splash of color.

24
00:01:58,240 --> 00:02:01,760
It sure is lonesome being
buried alive, but it's fine.

25
00:02:02,020 --> 00:02:04,667
I know Lamas will give
it her all to find me.

26
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:08,460
Oh Lamas, you've come such a long way.

27
00:02:08,760 --> 00:02:09,597
When we met,

28
00:02:09,680 --> 00:02:13,357
other hunters thought you were useless and
you'd even been abandoned by your team.

29
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:16,146
I'm sure that must have
hurt like the dickens.

30
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:18,817
But check out your glow up.

31
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:22,777
Now you're an able hunter and a household
name in the clear flow lake stratum.

32
00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:25,177
I've literally had your
back this whole time.

33
00:02:25,260 --> 00:02:28,084
So just thinking about
it gets me all verklempt.

34
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:30,880
She told me we could
stay together forever.

35
00:02:31,820 --> 00:02:33,217
Once this little mess is settled.

36
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:37,829
I have no doubt she'll help me conquer
another dungeon to become human again.

37
00:02:38,260 --> 00:02:40,437
Seems the rest of the gang
wants to tag along too.

38
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:41,820
Road trip baby.

39
00:02:42,380 --> 00:02:46,517
As long as I can keep adventuring with
this rowdy yet lovable band of misfits,

40
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:47,953
I've got no complaints.

41
00:02:49,100 --> 00:02:50,560
Welp, time for the yuge.

42
00:02:50,740 --> 00:02:53,757
I'll show these meanies what
vending machines are made of.

43
00:02:53,840 --> 00:03:05,423
Come over there!

44
00:03:05,506 --> 00:03:06,336
Fox Show!

45
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:19,637
On the outside, I'm just a big metal box,
but inside, I've still got a human soul!

46
00:03:19,720 --> 00:03:21,177
In this new world of wonders,

47
00:03:21,260 --> 00:03:24,757
I travel to and fro on the back
of my super strong partner, Lamas!

48
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:26,840
The name's Boxxo! Hello there!

49
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:28,680
That means yes, by the way!

50
00:03:41,900 --> 00:03:43,520
My poison cry.

51
00:03:43,880 --> 00:03:44,820
You can kill...

52
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:47,000
Oh...

53
00:03:49,240 --> 00:03:50,157
I'm not put down...

54
00:03:50,240 --> 00:03:51,070
I'm not put down...

55
00:03:51,153 --> 00:03:52,197
I don't feel...

56
00:03:52,280 --> 00:03:54,617
I really don't have a clue... Here...

57
00:03:54,700 --> 00:03:55,777
I'm not gonna be a scene.

58
00:03:55,860 --> 00:03:57,460
I'm not looking at vibe.

59
00:03:58,420 --> 00:03:59,957
Don't go anywhere...

60
00:04:00,040 --> 00:04:01,097
I'll have a lot of fun...

61
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:02,020
You can't...

62
00:04:02,820 --> 00:04:04,917
If you let, you play...

63
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:06,137
The only time you got into the mode...

64
00:04:06,220 --> 00:04:09,737
You can't lose...

65
00:04:09,820 --> 00:04:11,291
I'm holding a dream self.

66
00:04:12,060 --> 00:04:14,500
And I know what I have left.

67
00:04:14,640 --> 00:04:18,620
I'm holding a dream in the dark.

68
00:04:19,440 --> 00:04:22,017
I'm holding my head head.

69
00:04:22,100 --> 00:04:23,257
I'm holding my head.

70
00:04:23,340 --> 00:04:26,220
I'm holding my thigh.

71
00:04:28,580 --> 00:04:32,840
What can I have left?

72
00:04:33,700 --> 00:04:35,120
I'm holding my head.

73
00:04:50,740 --> 00:04:51,720
Hello there.

74
00:04:51,980 --> 00:04:52,860
Hello there.

75
00:04:53,120 --> 00:04:54,000
Hello there.

76
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:55,420
That voice.

77
00:04:57,300 --> 00:04:58,130
Bobco!

78
00:04:58,213 --> 00:04:59,340
I'm on my way!

79
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:01,840
It's Lovas!

80
00:05:02,380 --> 00:05:03,210
Bobco!

81
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:04,900
Hello there.

82
00:05:05,080 --> 00:05:06,060
Bob, I knew it!

83
00:05:06,540 --> 00:05:07,952
You hang in there, okay?

84
00:05:08,060 --> 00:05:09,236
I'm digging you out!

85
00:05:13,100 --> 00:05:15,180
Oh, phew, glad you're not squished.

86
00:05:15,360 --> 00:05:16,637
Good to have you back.

87
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:18,717
Everyone's feeling worried sick about you.

88
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:21,153
We should have known you'd be just fine.

89
00:05:24,520 --> 00:05:26,400
I missed you so much.

90
00:05:26,580 --> 00:05:27,957
You're not broken, are you?

91
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:29,200
Or scratched up?

92
00:05:30,040 --> 00:05:31,360
I was so... Honestly,

93
00:05:31,580 --> 00:05:32,977
you're lucky to be in one piece,

94
00:05:33,060 --> 00:05:35,157
but you don't always have
to push your luck, you know.

95
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:36,070
Yes.

96
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:38,137
We finally made it.

97
00:05:38,220 --> 00:05:39,700
How's it going, Boxo?

98
00:05:39,880 --> 00:05:42,597
Is it too soon to ask you
to dish out some snacks?

99
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:44,980
Boxo's been dug out, can you dig it?

100
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:47,977
I always knew you'd make
it out of this, okay, pal?

101
00:05:48,060 --> 00:05:50,140
Beyond a shadow of a doubt!

102
00:05:51,340 --> 00:05:54,317
Your humor leaves a lot to
be desired, Director Dog.

103
00:05:54,400 --> 00:05:55,260
Hey, Boxo.

104
00:05:55,460 --> 00:05:56,695
It's good to see you.

105
00:05:57,060 --> 00:06:00,648
The directors are safe and sound,
but wait, where's the bear?

106
00:06:01,420 --> 00:06:03,440
Well, it's every when.

107
00:06:03,780 --> 00:06:05,800
Oh, all of our friends are safe.

108
00:06:06,020 --> 00:06:07,617
Director Bear and the others are busy.

109
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:09,657
They're pursuing the monster horde.

110
00:06:09,740 --> 00:06:12,940
Knowing my buddies are okay
is a huge load off my ram.

111
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:14,900
Now, time to get vending.

112
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:20,757
Seeing as how the town was destroyed,
there aren't a ton of food options.

113
00:06:20,840 --> 00:06:22,900
This calls for a lavish feast.

114
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:24,160
Hello there.

115
00:06:24,660 --> 00:06:28,037
There's plenty to go around, so
just wait your turn, everyone.

116
00:06:28,120 --> 00:06:29,640
And remember, be fair.

117
00:06:29,820 --> 00:06:31,377
Children and old people go first.

118
00:06:31,460 --> 00:06:33,117
So don't try to cut the line.

119
00:06:33,200 --> 00:06:34,141
Hello, everyone.

120
00:06:34,320 --> 00:06:35,150
Want some free food?

121
00:06:35,233 --> 00:06:38,376
Trust me, you're gonna flip
when you taste this stuff!

122
00:06:41,980 --> 00:06:46,460
In the end, I doled out packaged prezis
until the wee hours of the morning.

123
00:06:47,400 --> 00:06:50,871
Pretty sure we've got enough
boxo food to last a while now.

124
00:06:51,160 --> 00:06:52,300
A job well done.

125
00:06:52,560 --> 00:06:56,501
Since they're not gonna starve, we
can go catch up with the others.

126
00:06:57,520 --> 00:07:01,344
I'm told Captain Carry Oil's family
went after the monster horde.

127
00:07:01,720 --> 00:07:03,191
Meanwhile, Director Bear,

128
00:07:03,300 --> 00:07:04,130
the guards,

129
00:07:04,213 --> 00:07:08,568
Heavy, and Mishuel are in a mad dash to
beat the beasts to the fortified city.

130
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:12,602
You better make sure you take a
little break if you need to, Boxo.

131
00:07:13,820 --> 00:07:14,760
I agree.

132
00:07:15,180 --> 00:07:16,100
Just relax.

133
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:18,080
Live a little, Boxo.

134
00:07:19,640 --> 00:07:21,287
Take your hands to yourself!

135
00:07:21,440 --> 00:07:22,717
We know you've been through a lot,

136
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:25,317
so it's probably a good idea
to take it easy for a bit.

137
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:26,580
Oh, thank you.

138
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:28,240
They need to rest.

139
00:07:28,420 --> 00:07:30,217
Those four stayed up all night with me.

140
00:07:30,300 --> 00:07:32,437
But I won't stop till the job is done.

141
00:07:32,520 --> 00:07:34,980
You never change, do you, kiddo? Huh?

142
00:07:47,320 --> 00:07:50,377
Getting so old you wake up
early does have its perks.

143
00:07:50,460 --> 00:07:53,225
My skin's not porcinum,
but aging's not so bad.

144
00:07:53,520 --> 00:07:54,755
Collagen's overrated.

145
00:07:56,980 --> 00:07:59,260
The senior squad came equipped.

146
00:07:59,520 --> 00:08:00,977
He thinks they want to tag along.

147
00:08:01,060 --> 00:08:02,620
Count me in too, big boy.

148
00:08:03,020 --> 00:08:04,520
I'm getting fired up.

149
00:08:04,860 --> 00:08:07,437
Guess they're coming
along for the ride too.

150
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:09,557
I hate getting up early.

151
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:11,217
You sound like a spoiled brat.

152
00:08:11,300 --> 00:08:14,037
Splash some water on your face
and pull yourself together, boy.

153
00:08:14,120 --> 00:08:15,080
I don't want to.

154
00:08:15,520 --> 00:08:17,100
Our team will remain here.

155
00:08:17,300 --> 00:08:19,720
We'll work on rebuilding the town. Nice.

156
00:08:19,980 --> 00:08:21,877
Now I don't have to
worry about this place.

157
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:24,078
I know I'm leaving it in good hands.

158
00:08:26,080 --> 00:08:28,457
Why do men always sneak
away in the morning?

159
00:08:28,540 --> 00:08:29,860
We'll miss you, Boxo.

160
00:08:30,200 --> 00:08:32,280
Lamy, please be careful out there.

161
00:08:32,420 --> 00:08:34,257
Be sure to give him help for us.

162
00:08:34,340 --> 00:08:36,160
Thank you. Sneak you.

163
00:08:36,740 --> 00:08:39,380
Well, is everyone ready
to get going? Yeah!

164
00:08:45,020 --> 00:08:48,432
Isn't it a tad silly to be
hiding behind a tree like that?

165
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:51,060
Oh, goodness.

166
00:08:51,480 --> 00:08:53,774
I didn't think you'd be able to see me.

167
00:08:56,400 --> 00:08:58,177
Pleased to make your acquaintance,

168
00:08:58,260 --> 00:09:02,554
and I deeply apologize for all the
trouble my naughty son has caused you.

169
00:09:04,620 --> 00:09:05,855
Who the heck are you?

170
00:09:05,940 --> 00:09:08,317
And who's this alleged
son you're talking about?

171
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:09,720
Oh, how spicy.

172
00:09:10,180 --> 00:09:11,298
Ribby's pernicious.

173
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:13,421
He's my little rascal, after all.

174
00:09:14,080 --> 00:09:17,497
Uh, lady, not to be mean, but is
Ribby in the room with us right now?

175
00:09:17,580 --> 00:09:20,757
When he was a child, he was
so quiet and mild-mannered.

176
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:24,417
Where do you suppose I went wrong
for him to turn out the way he did?

177
00:09:24,500 --> 00:09:25,680
I almost forgot.

178
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:29,337
Little Ribby, I hear he goes
by a different name these days.

179
00:09:29,420 --> 00:09:33,220
I think it was, oh, now I
remember, the Netherlord.

180
00:09:35,780 --> 00:09:37,480
The Nether Mama showed up?

181
00:09:37,580 --> 00:09:38,992
Talk about a plot twist.

182
00:09:46,520 --> 00:09:48,220
I know kids like to rebel,

183
00:09:48,440 --> 00:09:52,087
but I still can't believe he
experimented on his own mother to

184
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:54,757
get that skeleton body.

185
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:58,037
As if that weren't bad enough,
he also won't let me die.

186
00:09:58,120 --> 00:09:59,640
How could he be so cruel?

187
00:10:00,020 --> 00:10:04,440
He used his own mother as a test
subject for his twisted dark art.

188
00:10:05,860 --> 00:10:10,880
Damn, Netherlord, I knew you were mega-scum,
but this is full-on psycho territory.

189
00:10:11,440 --> 00:10:15,257
Of course, a mother's love is eternal,
so I forgive him for everything!

190
00:10:15,340 --> 00:10:17,497
Now I'm the Thumb
General and I strike down

191
00:10:17,580 --> 00:10:20,060
anyone who dares to stand in my son's way!

192
00:10:20,400 --> 00:10:21,800
I'm a good mother!

193
00:10:22,400 --> 00:10:25,929
Alright, so just to be clear,
are you gonna try and kill us?

194
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:28,120
Of course I am!

195
00:10:28,300 --> 00:10:31,418
A mother's love is nothing
if it's not unconditional!

196
00:10:33,100 --> 00:10:35,477
That's a lovely maternal
sentiment on paper,

197
00:10:35,560 --> 00:10:37,972
but it doesn't entail aiding mass murder!

198
00:10:38,500 --> 00:10:41,117
Seems to me you're a
sorry excuse for a mother.

199
00:10:41,200 --> 00:10:45,337
When a child's misbehaving, it's a
mother's duty to smack some sense into us.

200
00:10:45,420 --> 00:10:49,437
The situation you just described isn't
a mother's love, it's indulgence.

201
00:10:49,520 --> 00:10:50,560
Don't say that!

202
00:10:50,780 --> 00:10:53,357
How dare you condemn me when
I've given him everything!

203
00:10:53,440 --> 00:10:56,297
Don't you fool see that I'm
the best mother there ever was?

204
00:10:56,380 --> 00:10:59,498
Everyone in the world except
my ribby and me can die!

205
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:02,353
The apple didn't fall far from the tree.

206
00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:05,777
There's clearly no point trying
to reason with the thumb general

207
00:11:05,860 --> 00:11:08,625
Anyone who isn't fighting,
follow me to safety.

208
00:11:24,400 --> 00:11:27,400
Did you think we'd let
you get away with this?

209
00:11:30,980 --> 00:11:33,297
You cowards are ganging up on me!

210
00:11:33,380 --> 00:11:34,957
It's inexcusable.

211
00:11:35,040 --> 00:11:37,600
John, it's feeding time.

212
00:11:39,620 --> 00:11:41,337
That looks like the summoning circle.

213
00:11:41,420 --> 00:11:42,397
The netherlord used.

214
00:11:42,480 --> 00:11:44,421
Pretty clear where this is going.

215
00:11:45,060 --> 00:11:48,097
I've got a real bad feeling
about that summoning circle.

216
00:11:48,180 --> 00:11:49,317
So watch your back.

217
00:11:49,400 --> 00:11:50,637
Come on, gramps!

218
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:52,157
Could it really be that bad?

219
00:11:52,240 --> 00:11:55,077
It could that mana is downright alien.

220
00:11:55,160 --> 00:11:57,377
It may be a monster from another.

221
00:11:57,460 --> 00:11:59,660
Holy Isekai!

222
00:12:00,760 --> 00:12:03,054
What's that weird monster-shaped thing?

223
00:12:03,540 --> 00:12:08,246
I've seen more than my fair share of
monsters here, but that thing's ridiculous!

224
00:12:10,540 --> 00:12:12,460
Boxxo! Boxxo! Boxxo!

225
00:12:22,220 --> 00:12:23,050
Boxxo?

226
00:12:23,440 --> 00:12:24,360
Oh, wow!

227
00:12:27,460 --> 00:12:29,636
You can leave this nasty fella to us.

228
00:12:29,760 --> 00:12:31,957
We're all itching to get in on the action.

229
00:12:32,040 --> 00:12:35,957
Once you get as old as we are, you're
too short on time to bother with fear.

230
00:12:36,040 --> 00:12:39,117
I don't know, the two of you still
find ways to scare me occasionally.

231
00:12:39,200 --> 00:12:41,847
It does get intense when
you two are arguing.

232
00:12:42,020 --> 00:12:43,937
Oh yeah, now I'm doubly fired up.

233
00:12:44,020 --> 00:12:46,597
The forces of justice
fighting back against evil?

234
00:12:46,680 --> 00:12:48,915
Yeah, this is what dreams are made of!

235
00:12:58,160 --> 00:12:59,040
Shimmer down.

236
00:13:00,560 --> 00:13:02,477
Oh, things are getting hot in here.

237
00:13:02,560 --> 00:13:06,384
Looks like these buggies like to
explode whenever you blast them.

238
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:12,300
Hey, what the hey?

239
00:13:12,640 --> 00:13:15,877
If this becomes a war of attrition,
stamina could be a real problem.

240
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:20,017
If only I could distract our opponent
with some kind of elaborate display.

241
00:13:20,100 --> 00:13:22,276
Wait, I'm a freaking vending machine!

242
00:13:29,440 --> 00:13:31,440
I tend it up!

243
00:13:39,660 --> 00:13:40,940
I, er, work!

244
00:13:41,760 --> 00:13:42,590
Freddie!

245
00:13:42,840 --> 00:13:44,369
The whole sky's sparkling!

246
00:13:44,980 --> 00:13:47,017
Fireworks are always something special,

247
00:13:47,100 --> 00:13:49,597
but there's nothing like
your very first time.

248
00:13:49,680 --> 00:13:50,856
There's the big bug.

249
00:13:50,980 --> 00:13:52,317
It's not really advancing,

250
00:13:52,400 --> 00:13:55,757
but it's also facing away from
the fireworks, which means...

251
00:13:55,840 --> 00:13:57,500
My hunch was right.

252
00:13:57,740 --> 00:14:01,387
The Thumb General is the one
pulling its gross little strings.

253
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:05,120
Simply gorgeous. Lock it. Huh?

254
00:14:05,280 --> 00:14:06,986
Did you need something, Boxo?

255
00:14:07,580 --> 00:14:09,820
You hit it for O. Yup.

256
00:14:10,060 --> 00:14:11,217
Now that I'm ranked three,

257
